A||||4||Hybrid2M6||How would you fix...||||5||
Z||000000||Hybrid2M6||11-19-2001||01:32 PM||||How would you fix a hole that goes all the way thru your deck lid? Kinda like if you took off your luggage rack and slapped on an insanley huge wing. Anyways I started with sanding around the holes and then using a fiberglass repair kit, cut piece and placed them over the holes. After I sande over the hole lid as I plan to ad a ferrarimomo scoop. Am I close? Help me out please.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-19-2001||01:40 PM||||thats how i filled my antenna, and badging holes.. use S glass if you can instead of E glass.. it's a bit more expensive but will flex with the body. available at  <A HREF="http://www.aircraftspruce.com" TARGET=_blank>www.aircraftspruce.com</A>   they carry all kinds of great things... <P>(off topic -  how do you like your Azenis'? we've got a set on the Regional 3rd place SCCA Solo SM Turbo Focus here, i love to drive that car but they seem noisier than my Paradas)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||11-19-2001||01:43 PM||||Chamfer the hole about 1/2" beyond it's edges.  Back it up from the underside with tape, etc.  Fill the hole with fibreglass resin.  While its still wet, lay some wetted matting on top in the chamferred hole.  Let it all harden up, sand it flat, paint.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hybrid2M6||11-19-2001||01:47 PM||||Thanks guys. As for the Azenis tires, I love em. Thought they would suck in the rain due to lack of tread, but the stick better than when I had the Ziex 502's on the rear.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||6
Z||000004||ka4nkf||11-22-2001||01:55 AM||||If you don't do like watts said the filling in the hole will pop out after a while.||||reg||1
